---
import brandMarkImg from '../assets/logo-mark.webp';
import { getImage } from 'astro:assets';
import { parseEventDate, formatEventDateRange, getEventTypeLabel } from '../lib/events';
import { parseVideoId } from '../lib/platforms/youtube';
import { buildImageSet } from '../lib/local-content';

/*
  ─── `wide` ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  This card is a horizontal row, and it was built for a 3-up grid: /events and
  /events/archive both hand it a `.event-grid` track around 420-450px, where
  a stacked meta / title / CTA fills the body edge to edge.

  A hub's "Upcoming Events" list is not that. A hub typically has ONE upcoming
  event, so in the same 3-up grid it rendered a single row card in the left
  third with two empty tracks beside it. Filling the width instead leaves the
  opposite problem: a 130px image and a left-hugging text stack with a thousand
  pixels of nothing after it.

  So `wide` re-anchors the row for full-bleed: meta and title stay left, the
  CTA moves to the far right, and the card is pinned at both ends. It also
  swaps the meta's year for the actual date range, which is the fact that
  matters when the event has not happened yet ("Oct 8-11", not "2026").

  Opt-in on purpose. The two archive grids pass nothing and are untouched.
*/
const { event, index = 0, wide = false } = Astro.props;
const brandMarkImgOptimized = await getImage({ src: brandMarkImg, format: 'webp' });
const trailerId = parseVideoId(event.trailerUrl);

/*
  ─── THE EYEBROW SAYS WHAT THE EVENT IS ────────────────────────────────────

  This was the literal string "Event" on every card, which is a placeholder
  wearing the clothes of metadata: the store has carried an `eventType` on all
  nineteen events since they were classified, and the hero tag on the event's
  own page has been reading it the whole time. A premiere said EVENT here and
  PREMIERE one click later.

  `getEventTypeLabel` is the same resolver those pages use, and it already
  falls back to 'Event' for an unset type. So a card with no type on it renders
  exactly the string it used to.
*/
const typeLabel = getEventTypeLabel(event);

/* Upcoming events are announced by WHEN. Past ones, which is every other
   caller, are filed by year. */
const metaDate = wide
  ? formatEventDateRange(event.startDate, event.endDate)
  : (parseEventDate(event.startDate)?.year ?? 'Recent');

const hero = buildImageSet(event.heroImage, { widths: [320, 480, 640, 800], aspect: 16 / 9 });
const logo = buildImageSet(event.logo, { widths: [96, 160, 240] });


const imageSrc = logo?.src ?? hero?.src ?? (trailerId ? `https://img.youtube.com/vi/${trailerId}/hqdefault.jpg` : brandMarkImgOptimized.src);
const imageSrcset = logo?.srcset ?? hero?.srcset ?? undefined;
---

<a
  href={`/events/${event.slug.current}`}
  class:list={['content-card', 'past-event-card', 'group', 'animate-on-scroll', 'no-underline', { 'past-event-card--wide': wide }]}
  style={`--index: ${index};`}
>
  <div class="past-event-media">
    <img
      src={imageSrc}
      srcset={imageSrcset}
      sizes="120px"
      alt={event.title}
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async"
      class="past-event-img"
    />
  </div>

  <div class="past-event-body">
    {/*
      Meta and title are ONE block, deliberately.

      Without this wrapper the wide row's `justify-content: space-between` had
      three children to distribute, so the title landed dead centre with a gulf
      on either side of it. That is the orphaned-card problem again, moved
      inside the card: the most important words on the row, anchored to
      nothing. Grouped, the row has two ends — identity on the left, action on
      the right — and the title sits against the logo where it belongs.

      Inert in the narrow layout. Both are flex containers, so no margin
      collapses and the stacked spacing is byte-for-byte what it was.
    */}
    <div class="past-event-text">
    {/*
      ─── ONE LINE OF METADATA, NOT THREE FLEX ITEMS ────────────────────

      This was a flex row of three spans. A flex item is a BOX, and a box
      that wraps internally keeps the width of its longest line — so at
      393px "Convention & Expo" broke to "CONVENTION &" / "EXPO", the box
      stayed 112px wide, and the bullet and year began after that box and
      centred against its 36px height. They landed beside the short second
      line with a gap in front of them, reading as though they belonged to
      nothing.

      It is text, so it flows as text now. The bullet and the year are one
      nowrap unit, which is what stops the other bad break: a line ending
      on a dangling separator.
    */}
    <div class="past-event-meta">
      <span>{typeLabel}</span>
      <span class="past-event-meta-date">
        <span aria-hidden="true">&bull;</span> {metaDate}
      </span>
    </div>

    <h3 class="past-event-title">{event.title}</h3>
    </div>

    {/*
      "View Coverage" is a promise, and on an UPCOMING event it is one nobody
      has made yet. The hub list is the only place this card shows events that
      have not happened, and whether they get covered is not decided when the
      card renders. Past events are the opposite case: the coverage is the
      reason the archive card exists, so it keeps the words it earned.

      "Event Details" is already the site's phrase for this, on the hub hero's
      own button.
    */}
    <span class="watch-now-btn">
      {wide ? 'Event Details' : 'View Coverage'} <span class="content-card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
      <span class="btn-underline"></span>
    </span>
  </div>
</a>

<style>
  .past-event-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    width: 100%;
    /*
      ─── THE MARK IS INSET, NOT FLUSH ───────────────────────────────────

      This was `padding: 0` with the note "edge to edge", which the media
      plate's own `background: #0a0a0a` was presumably meant to justify: a
      dark panel running into the card's border. On a #111 card that panel is
      invisible, so what actually reached the page was somebody's logo jammed
      against a hairline with nothing between them.

      The inline start now matches the body's own padding, so the mark is
      inset from the left border by the same distance the CTA is inset from
      the right one. The block edges stay at 0 and the plate still fills the
      card's full height.
    */
    padding: 0 0 0 1.5rem;
    gap: 0;
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    border-radius: 0; /* Sharp corners on the card */
    overflow: hidden;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: transform 0.3s ease, border-color 0.3s ease, box-shadow 0.3s ease;
  }

  .past-event-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-4px);
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 40px rgba(204, 0, 0, 0.15);
  }

  .past-event-card:hover .past-event-title {
    color: var(--color-white);
  }

  .past-event-card:hover .watch-now-btn {
    color: var(--color-accent-text);
  }

  .past-event-card:hover .btn-underline {
    width: 100%;
  }

  .past-event-media {
    flex: 0 0 130px; 
    height: 130px;
    padding: 1rem; 
    background: #0a0a0a; 
    border-radius: 0; 
    overflow: hidden;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  /* Typographic Fallback styling */
  .fallback-monogram {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a1a, #0a0a0a);
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);
    font-family: var(--font-display, 'Syne Variable', sans-serif);
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -1px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    /* A 326px card cannot spare 1.5rem on top of a 90px plate and still leave
       the title a readable measure. */
    .past-event-card,
    .past-event-card--wide {
      padding-left: 1rem;
    }
    .past-event-media {
      flex: 0 0 90px;
      height: 90px;
      padding: 0.5rem;
    }
    .past-event-title {
      font-size: 1.1rem;
    }
    .fallback-monogram {
      font-size: 1.8rem;
    }
  }

  .past-event-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: contain;
    transition: transform 0.5s ease;
  }

  .past-event-card:hover .past-event-img {
    transform: scale(1.05);
  }

  .past-event-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
    flex: 1;
  }

  .past-event-text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .past-event-meta {
    color: #a1a1aa;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
    /*
      Block, not flex. The three parts are a single line of metadata and
      should wrap like one — see the note on the markup for what the flex
      row did to a label too long for the card.
    */
    display: block;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  /*
    The separator belongs to the date, never to the end of a line.

    The gap is a margin, not the whitespace between the two spans: Astro
    collapses that away at build time, and the pair rendered as
    "Convention• 2026". 0.4rem is what the flex `gap` used to contribute.
  */
  .past-event-meta-date {
    white-space: nowrap;
    margin-left: 0.4rem;
  }

  .past-event-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-white);
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem 0;
  }

  /* Was `style="margin-top: 0.6rem"` on the element. An inline style cannot be
     overridden by a class, and the wide row needs this gap gone. */
  .past-event-card .watch-now-btn {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
  }

  /*
    ─── THE WIDE ROW ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    One card across the full content width, so it is anchored at BOTH ends:
    the text stack stays left against the image, the CTA sits hard right. The
    gap between them is the row, not dead space at the end of it.
  */
  /* The wide row's body carries 1.75rem, so its mark is inset to match. */
  .past-event-card--wide {
    padding-left: 1.75rem;
  }

  .past-event-card--wide .past-event-body {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 2rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.75rem;
  }

  .past-event-card--wide .past-event-title {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* Left block hugs the logo and takes what it needs; the CTA keeps its own
     width and the slack falls between them, which is where slack should go. */
  .past-event-card--wide .past-event-text {
    flex: 0 1 auto;
  }

  .past-event-card--wide .watch-now-btn {
    margin-top: 0;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  /*
    Below the grid's own breakpoint the row runs out of width for two anchors,
    so it goes back to the stack it already knows how to be. Left aligned, not
    centred: the image is still on the left edge of the card, and centred text
    beside a left-aligned image reads as a mistake.
  */
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .past-event-card--wide .past-event-body {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      justify-content: center;
      gap: 0;
      padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    }
    .past-event-card--wide .past-event-title {
      margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    }
    .past-event-card--wide .watch-now-btn {
      margin-top: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
